watch-spin-new-router — rowt #s105, the spin heal's sample.

The machine is use-auto-unchanged's with the router up (host.pid.self) and a
steady-state tick: watch.net and the proxy getters unchanged, the corp lane
already synced, the bypass list right, the auto probe answering. So the tick
reaches the healthy branch of the health check, the one place the spin heal
runs. The clash API reports no byte totals, so the traffic sample is 0 B/s.
watch.cpu names the stand-in router as @ROUTER_PID@ and its time as
@NOW-<s>@; the harness fills both, and masks the epoch and pid fields when it
compares the tree (snap_norm).

Here the last sample names another pid (1): the router was restarted since,
so there is no interval to average over. Expected: watch.cpu rewritten with
this router's sample, watch.cpustreak removed, nothing logged.
